    {
      "id": "authoring-switches-intro",
      "type": "content",
      "label": "intro",
      "position": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 340
      },
      "width": 1100,
      "height": 560,
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "# Authoring switches\n\n**A draft, for Michael to edit.** What a person can set on a node or a graph to change how it looks or behaves, which of those the Properties panel offers, where each is written down, and how a Method can set them.\n\n**Setting one from a Method.** The script API is generic (`updateNode`, `updateView`, `createNode`, `applyDeltas`), so any switch below can be written by a Method that declares the effect that allows it. What is missing is not functions but a list: which switches exist, what each does, and the effect path that writes it.\n\n**How this list was made.** From a scan of the code and the docs, so it is a first pass: a switch marked \"no\" under Panel or Documented was not found there, not proven absent. Check a row before relying on it.\n\n**How to read it.** *Panel*: a control in the Properties panel. *Written down*: where (AGENTS.md, SCRIPTING.md, a primitive page)."
        },
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "authoring-switches"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "authoring-switches-table",
      "type": "content",
      "label": "table",
      "position": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 940
      },
      "width": 1100,
      "height": 760,
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "## The switches\n\n| Switch | What it does | Panel | Written down |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `visible` | hides a node in browse mode; it always shows while editing | yes | AGENTS.md |\n| `visibilityRole` | meant to set browse visibility, but cannot override the type rule | no | AGENTS.md, as a warning |\n| `positionLocked` | pins a ground behind every other node | no | one line, AGENTS.md |\n| `showLabel`, `hideLabel` | a node's label; a handle's sign | no | no |\n| `rotation` | turns a node, and its handles with it | no | partly, docs |\n| `semanticLevel`, `semanticZoom` | which view a node shows at which size | no | no |\n| `handlePresentation`, `handleRef` | the art a Port wears | no | AGENTS.md |\n| `defaultHandle` (on the root) | the art every Port the graph exposes wears | no | AGENTS.md |\n| `view.fit: 'window'` | the environment follows the graph window | no | AGENTS.md |\n| `view.scroll: 'page'` | a Detail is a page that scrolls | no | no |\n| `membrane.bounds` | the graph window's crop; turns the automatic box off | no | AGENTS.md |\n| `renderShape` | a shape hint | yes | AGENTS.md says do not use it in new graphs |\n| `autoRunOnLoad`, `autoRunOnGraphChange` | when a Method runs by itself | yes | no |\n| `allowMutations`, `dryRun` | whether a Method may write, or only report | yes | no |"
        },
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "authoring-switches"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "authoring-switches-missing",
      "type": "content",
      "label": "missing",
      "position": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 1740
      },
      "width": 1100,
      "height": 900,
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "## What is missing\n\nThese are not switches yet, or are not findable. In the order I would do them.\n\n1. **Show in browse mode.** Nothing can make a root, a face or a glyph show while browsing. `visible: true` does not, because it is the default on every node and the type rule runs first. Proposed: `data.showInBrowse: true`, set only on the primitive pages, so a reader sees the real root and views the page is about.\n2. **Root handle on a tile.** A graph's implicit root Port is where a portal lands by default, and a workspace tile does not draw it. Proposed: drawn by default, on the left, as a plain disc unless the Declaration names a Handle; `root.handle: 'hidden'` turns it off.\n3. **`semanticLevel` and `semanticZoom`.** They decide what every tile looks like at each zoom, and nothing explains them.\n4. **One list.** AGENTS.md mentions a handful; SCRIPTING.md mentions none. This page, once edited, is the start of it.\n\n## Questions for Michael\n\n- Is `showInBrowse` the right name, and should it be a plain flag or one of `'browse'`, `'editor'`?\n- Should the root handle show on every tile by default, or only where a graph asks?\n- Where should the finished list live: a canon page, a glossary entry, or both?"
        },
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "authoring-switches"
        }
      }
    }
